course: dictionary
lesson: 6473
title: Natural and what it means
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word natural has several meanings, so the words around it tell you which one to use. In «It's natural to feel nervous», natural means normal or expected, so lots of people feel that way.
explain: If the sentence is about nature, materials or the world around us, natural means made by nature, not by people or machines, like natural light or natural rock. Swap in "made by nature" and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Natural can also mean not fake, or being very good at something without trying hard. The phrase «natural leader» can be spin, which means choosing nice-sounding words to make something sound better than it is, so read the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: Natural means made by nature, not by people or machines.
fact: Natural also means normal or expected, as in «It's natural to feel nervous».
fact: A natural is an informal word for someone who is very good at something without trying hard.
fact: In maths, the natural numbers are the counting numbers 1, 2, 3, and some books also include 0.
fact: Natural materials like wood, wool and stone come from nature, while plastic and nylon are man-made.
exercise: «Coal, oil and natural gas are fossil fuels formed over millions of years.» What does natural mean here? | Expected by everyone | Fake | Very quick | *Made by nature, not by people
exercise: «It's natural to feel nervous before a test.» What does natural mean here? | A kind of rock | Very loud | Made of plastic | *Normal and expected
exercise: «Sunflowers grow, flower, make seeds and die, which is their natural life.» What does natural life mean? | A fake life in a pot | *The normal way a plant lives | A life spent in a shop | A life with no seeds
test: «Natural disasters are earthquakes, floods and hurricanes.» What does natural mean here? | Expected by everyone | *Caused by nature | Caused by people | Very tiny
test: Maya says, «She's a natural at drawing, and she never even practises.» What is a natural? | Someone who has just left home | Someone who is fake | *Someone who is very good without trying hard | A type of plastic
exam: Which of these is man-made, not natural? | Wood | Stone | *Nylon | Wool
